    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0841" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg709"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7411: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-26T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26, 1926—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>107. Your telegram No. 226, May 23, 2 p.m. Instructions suggested in second
                    paragraph of your telegram are approved.</p>
                <p>The Department considers it preferable to have Mayer confer with Tredwell only at
                    Hongkong. However, in instructions sent to Tredwell<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d574-f1"/> he is authorized to go to Canton if Mayer so requests. If
                    you consider it necessary you may authorize Chamberlain to go to Canton for
                    conference with Mayer.</p>
                <p>The Department prefers to have Mayer use commercial transportation. If commercial
                    transportation is available, no request will be made of the Navy.<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d574-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d574-f1" n="10" xml:id="d574-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d574-f2" n="11" xml:id="d574-f2-content">
                <p>Mayer left Peking May 31, and his arrival at Canton was reported June 12.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
